# Static Qt builds (Windows only)

Zarya on Windows **always** uses **static Qt**. There is no shared-Qt (`-Shared`) configure path.

## Configure and build

```powershell
.\scripts\configure-msvc2026.ps1
cmake --build build --config Release --target zarya
```

Or:

```powershell
.\scripts\build.ps1
```

Desktop App UI (`lib_ui`) is **always** linked. Requires OpenSSL and initialized `third_party/desktop-app` submodules.

## Static Qt location

- Prefix: `C:\Qt\Static\6.8.3\msvc2022_64`
- Override with `QT_STATIC_DIR` if installed elsewhere
- If missing, build once: `.\scripts\build-qt-static-msvc2026.ps1`
- CI restores a packed prefix (see `scripts/pack-qt-static-ci.ps1` / workflow `qt-static-windows`)

## Do not

- Do not configure Windows with shared/aqt Qt for app or release builds
- Do not change CMake to allow `ZARYA_STATIC_QT=OFF` on WIN32
